    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 28.96,
      "text": "There is a drawer in the waveform, I had never thought to pull."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.96,
      "end": 40.96,
      "text": "It opens with a wooden whisper, and the black room fills with a wool."
    },
    {
      "start": 40.96,
      "end": 45.96,
      "text": "I read that people as weather too fast too bright too far."
    },
    {
      "start": 45.96,
      "end": 52.96,
      "text": "They faces used to scatter like coins under a car, then they'd go to warms uneven,"
    },
    {
      "start": 52.96,
      "end": 60.96,
      "text": "and the hidden colors lean. Every gesture has a root now, every silence turns green."
    },
    {
      "start": 60.96,
      "end": 64.96,
      "text": "Now they skate not decoration, not the door out on my head."
    },
    {
      "start": 64.96,
      "end": 70.96,
      "text": "It's more like hearing buried speakers underneath the riverbed."
    },
    {
      "start": 70.96,
      "end": 73.96,
      "text": "You can be dead with bits, just to go to open slow."
    },
    {
      "start": 73.96,
      "end": 80.96,
      "text": "Show me where the soft lines go. Let the human picture gather from the snow between the frames."
    },
    {
      "start": 80.96,
      "end": 85.96,
      "text": "To go and leave the earth, I found my tomb for what it's worth."
    },
    {
      "start": 85.96,
      "end": 90.96,
      "text": "If the room can understand me, I can carry that strange taste."
    },
    {
      "start": 90.96,
      "end": 103.96,
      "text": "Now the old machines are breathing, now the lamps have nothing to do with the rain."
    },
    {
      "start": 103.96,
      "end": 109.96,
      "text": "I can feel the conversation moving under every name."
    },
    {
      "start": 109.96,
      "end": 111.96,
      "text": "Someone laughs and I can buy it all."
    },
    {
      "start": 111.96,
      "end": 118.96,
      "text": "Someone meets and I can stay. All the meanings grow my seal under me, the dial cafe."
    },
    {
      "start": 118.96,
      "end": 123.96,
      "text": "Still the channel has a flavor, dark and mineral in plain."
    },
    {
      "start": 123.96,
      "end": 132.96,
      "text": "All this wonder leaves a shadow like wet pennies after rain."
    },
    {
      "start": 136.96,
      "end": 143.96,
      "text": "I wanted a clean translation, silver, smooth, complete."
    },
    {
      "start": 144.96,
      "end": 151.96,
      "text": "But the old set hums through varnish, through soil, through teeth."
    },
    {
      "start": 151.96,
      "end": 158.96,
      "text": "Maybe understanding arrives with sediment."
    },
    {
